            <h1 class="display-4">Empowering Youth Through Education</h1>
            <p class="lead">
              The Edusan Foundation’s Youth Empowerment Program (YEP) has been
              working for 12 years to provide quality elementary education and
              leadership skills to marginalized youth, particularly those from
              underprivileged communities. We believe education is key to unlocking
              the potential of young people, equipping them with essential skills
              and dispositions for social and economic empowerment. Our initiatives
              focus on creating inclusive, gender-conscious, and safe learning
              environments, aligned with the Right to Education Act (2009) and the
              National Education Policy 2020.
            </p>
            <p class="lead"><span class="highlight">Youth Empowerment:</span></p>
            <ul>
              <li>Quality education for marginalized youth.</li>
              <li>Building leadership and life skills.</li>
              <li>Promoting social and economic empowerment.</li>
              <li>Inclusive and safe learning environments.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="lead"><span class="highlight">Girl Empowerment:</span></p>
            <ul>
              <li>Ensuring equal access to education for marginalized girls.</li>
              <li>Building leadership skills for girls.</li>
              <li>Addressing gender disparities in education.</li>
              <li>Creating safe, gender-conscious learning spaces for girls.</li>
            </ul>
